WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:03.747
You're making your Broadway debut in Meteor Shower.

2
00:00:03.747 --> 00:00:04.908
Yes.

3
00:00:04.908 --> 00:00:06.313
Yeah, this is exciting.

4
00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:08.864
(applause)

5
00:00:08.864 --> 00:00:11.686
Written by a scrappy young comic making his way up,

6
00:00:11.686 --> 00:00:12.800
named Steve Martin.

7
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.124
Big up-and-comer, Steve Martin.

8
00:00:14.124 --> 00:00:15.900
Big up-and-comer, yeah.

9
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.280
Haven't seen a lot of his stuff, but he was very promising.

10
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.975
Very promising.

11
00:00:19.975 --> 00:00:22.024
Yeah, it's been interesting, because in rehearsal,

12
00:00:22.024 --> 00:00:23.174
while we're rehearsing the play,

13
00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:25.043
they do tweaks every night, so like,

14
00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:27.736
we change things during the rehearsal during the day,

15
00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:29.304
so there are times when the director says,

16
00:00:29.304 --> 00:00:31.463
"So make sure, don't do the, don't do that move.

17
00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:32.624
"You're gonna do this move tonight."

18
00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:34.145
And then sometimes you're checking your phone,

19
00:00:34.145 --> 00:00:35.759
you're like, "No, got it, got it, got it."

20
00:00:35.759 --> 00:00:39.926
And then cut to 8:30 at night, and it's just like, you know.

21
00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:42.138
That's not...

22
00:00:43.459 --> 00:00:46.209
(Conan laughing)

23
00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:50.419
Forgot the, just forgot the moves.

24
00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:51.731
Yeah, you gotta walk that back.

25
00:00:51.731 --> 00:00:55.248
The lights come up, and you're like, "Oh!"

26
00:00:55.248 --> 00:00:58.513
(laughter and applause)

27
00:00:58.513 --> 00:01:01.416
Now, how do you handle, the thing that makes people crazy,

28
00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:04.817
a lot of actors, Broadway actors, say they can't stand

29
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:06.579
when people were talking in the crowd.

30
00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:07.450
Oh, gosh, yeah.

31
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.611
Have you experienced that?

32
00:01:08.611 --> 00:01:10.143
We have experienced it.

33
00:01:10.143 --> 00:01:14.067
I did a production of Hamlet at the Public Theater here

34
00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:15.844
in New York, earlier this year.

35
00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:17.376
(applause)

36
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:18.247
Serious play.

37
00:01:18.247 --> 00:01:19.605
And I'm sitting on the steps,

38
00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:22.078
like next to an an audience member, with Oscar Isaac,

39
00:01:22.078 --> 00:01:23.773
and Oscar Isaac, who is playing Hamlet,

40
00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:25.306
he sits down next to this woman.

41
00:01:25.306 --> 00:01:26.838
And this sweet little old woman,

42
00:01:26.838 --> 00:01:28.615
she's just looking at Oscar.

43
00:01:28.615 --> 00:01:30.855
And she just, as loud as she possibly can,

44
00:01:30.855 --> 00:01:34.861
she just goes, "Are they gonna carry you out?"

45
00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.322
(audience laughing)

46
00:01:37.322 --> 00:01:39.900
And he says, he goes, "I don't know.

47
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.955
"I don't know, but watch."

48
00:01:41.955 --> 00:01:43.754
And this same old woman, this same old woman,

49
00:01:43.754 --> 00:01:45.462
this poor lady, she was just havin' a day.

50
00:01:45.462 --> 00:01:46.295
Yeah.

51
00:01:46.295 --> 00:01:49.031
She was having a little bit of a time in the front row,

52
00:01:49.031 --> 00:01:50.679
and she was trying to be polite,

53
00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:52.839
so while a guy was doing a monologue, she was like,

54
00:01:52.839 --> 00:01:54.255
"I have to go to the bathroom.

55
00:01:54.255 --> 00:01:55.869
"I have to go to the bathroom."

56
00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:56.702
"Ma'am, you can wait."

57
00:01:56.702 --> 00:01:57.535
"I can't wait."

58
00:01:57.535 --> 00:01:58.368
"You can wait."

59
00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:01.035
And he stops speaking in the monologue so her,

60
00:02:01.035 --> 00:02:02.185
to get her voice up, he goes,

61
00:02:02.185 --> 00:02:05.435
"The time thus and has happened here."

62
00:02:05.435 --> 00:02:07.792
"I have to go number two!"

63
00:02:07.792 --> 00:02:11.125
(laughter and applause)

64
00:02:13.005 --> 00:02:13.899
It was amazing.

65
00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:16.128
But it's not, being an improv performer,

66
00:02:16.128 --> 00:02:18.032
you're used to people talking to you and stuff like that.

67
00:02:18.032 --> 00:02:20.238
It's like, even when you talk to them,

68
00:02:20.238 --> 00:02:21.643
then don't give you the response that you're

69
00:02:21.643 --> 00:02:22.476
always looking for.

70
00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:25.045
We've had people that come and watch the tapings,

71
00:02:25.045 --> 00:02:26.693
whether it was here in New York or in LA,

72
00:02:26.693 --> 00:02:29.178
and they're so used to watching the show on television.

73
00:02:29.178 --> 00:02:30.011
Yeah, yeah.

74
00:02:30.011 --> 00:02:31.244
That they'll be sitting there, and I'll come out,

75
00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:33.044
and they'll just go, very loudly,

76
00:02:33.044 --> 00:02:35.145
"He's taller than I thought!"

77
00:02:35.145 --> 00:02:36.678
(audience laughing)

78
00:02:36.678 --> 00:02:38.118
I'm here!

79
00:02:38.118 --> 00:02:38.951
Right, I'm right here.

80
00:02:38.951 --> 00:02:39.784
I'm here!

81
00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:41.090
And sometimes, I've gotten this, too.

82
00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.541
"Is he black?

83
00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:45.874
(laughter and applause)

84
00:02:48.009 --> 00:02:51.620
"The voice isn't black, is he Polynesian, Hispanic?

85
00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.560
"Where's he from?"

86
00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.428
Well, dammit, that was my next question.

87
00:02:55.428 --> 00:02:57.678
(applause)

88
00:03:01.442 --> 00:03:05.714
To answer the question, I've been half black for 46 years,

89
00:03:05.714 --> 00:03:09.151
and I'm all black when it's super convenient.

90
00:03:09.151 --> 00:03:11.972
(Conan laughing)

91
00:03:11.972 --> 00:03:16.105
Sometimes you have to be all black, sometimes.

92
00:03:16.105 --> 00:03:17.708
I didn't realize you had that power, all right.

93
00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:19.791
Yes, I have that power.

